  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "Reduced to lowest terms, \\[ \\frac{a^2-b^2}{ab}-\\frac{ab-b^2}{ab-a^2} \\] is equal to:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{a}{b}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{a^2-2b^2}{ab}\\)",
    "C": "\\(a^2\\)",
    "D": "\\(a-2b\\)",
    "E": "None of these answers"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The original denominators must be nonzero, so \\(a\\ne0\\), \\(b\\ne0\\), and \\(a\\ne b\\). Factor the second fraction to reveal a common factor:\n\\[\n\\frac{ab-b^2}{ab-a^2}\n=\\frac{b(a-b)}{-a(a-b)}\n=-\\frac ba.\n\\]\nCancelling \\(a-b\\) is valid because \\(a\\ne b\\). Subtracting this negative fraction now gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{a^2-b^2}{ab}-\\left(-\\frac ba\\right)\n&=\\frac{a^2-b^2}{ab}+\\frac{b^2}{ab}\\\\\n&=\\frac{a^2}{ab}\\\\\n&=\\frac ab.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus the reduced expression is \\(\\boxed{a/b}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\), with the original restrictions retained.",
